  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/approach.rs`: a new field `Approach::approach_distance` (mm). The default is `DEFAULT_APPROACH_DISTANCE` = 2.0. `Approach::approach_distance_refusal()` refuses a negative, non-finite or too large value by name. `Approach::validate` calls it.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/types/sane.rs`: `named_refusal` gives that refusal, so `CreateOperation` and `EditOperationParams` refuse a bad value with its name. Before this, the refusal was only the general \"operation parameters are not usable\".\n- `crates/app/src/project/approach.rs`: the optional file key `approach_distance`. The file writes it only when the value is not the default. A file without the key loads the default. The project format version does not change (the serde default law), so this change is not breaking.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/params/digest.rs`: the digest adds bytes only for a value that is not the default. The digest of each earlier operation does not change.\n- UI (`approach_page.rs`, `kind_editors.rs`, `mill2d_page.rs`): the Lead in / Lead out tab of 2D Offset, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive shows an \"Approach\" group with the row \"Approach distance\" and a hover tooltip. The row shows only when Pass starts at is Inside or Outside.\n- MCP: `edit_operation` and `add_operation` set the value through `links.approach.approach_distance` (the same params door, the same undoable command). `get_job` reads it. `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` has a new row.\n- `docs/decisions/3745-approach-distance.md`: the default and its reason.\n\nNo change to the ring planner (#3744) or to the entry. The entry sub-issue #3746 reads the value. Until then the value is stored and changes no move.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `mcp_approach_distance::approach_distance_default_is_two_mm_and_writes_no_key` (the default)\n- `mcp_approach_distance::mcp_sets_approach_distance_and_refuses_a_negative_value` (MCP set and get; refusal of -1.0, -0.001 on edit and -2.0 on add, by name, with no change to the job)\n- `mcp_approach_distance::approach_distance_edit_undoes_and_redoes` (undo and redo through `EditOperationParams`)\n- `mcp_approach_distance::approach_distance_round_trips_through_save_and_load` (save and load keep the value; a file without the key loads the default)\n- `lead_approach::the_stamp_tells_the_approach_apart_and_a_default_op_keeps_its_digest` (one new case: a changed approach distance changes the digest)\n- `egui_app::tests::pass_start::the_leads_tab_shows_the_approach_distance_only_for_inside_and_outside` (UI structural: the row is present for Inside and Outside, absent for Auto, on Pocket, Offset2D and Adaptive2D)\n\n## Gate\n\n- The pinning tests above: green (`cargo xtask gate test`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`).\n- `lead_approach::the_approach_round_trips_and_the_defaults_write_no_key`: green.\n- `ui suites: lib` (all camcraft-ui lib tests): green.\n- `motion suites: lib`: green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not run: the full quick plan. The motion diff reaches 1186 steps (every app and ui binary), so it is not a quick run. The batch gate on main covers it after the merge.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. No toolpath or post output changes: the value has no reader yet.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No app window was opened. The tooltip text is not asserted (egui puts a hover text in the tree only on hover).\n- 3D Pocket, 3D Finish, Bore and Circular do not show the row. #3746 decides which kinds read the value.\n\nProcess change: yes (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`)\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The Lead in / Lead out page has an Approach distance (default 2 mm) for passes that start Inside or Outside: how far outside the stock edge the tool goes down to the cut depth. It is saved in the project, undoable, and settable over MCP as `links.approach.approach_distance`.\n\nFixes #3745\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
